 "verdict": "NO BALL JOINT EXISTS IN THIS GEOMETRY. 82 spherical patches were fitted on placed geometry (41 balls, 39 sockets, 2 mixed). 6 ball/socket pairs came within 0.6 mm of concentric and every one is refuted below by its own measurement. The spherical features in this robot are dome ends of printed pockets, drill points, fillet caps and the toroidal chamfers of the bearing rings \u2014 not articulating joints. Leif named ball joints; the geometry does not contain one, and that is a measurement, not a refusal to look.",
